{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/781602-alternative-demon-lores-and-powers","id":781602,"title":"Alternative Demon Lores and Powers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-07T01:09:32-08:00","id":781602,"title":"Alternative Demon Lores and Powers","content":"After reading this thread: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/656937-demon-lores-are-meh\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-lores-are-meh</a><br /> I got the idea, of making an alternative system for the &quot;magic&quot; of the fallen.<br /> The base Problem is the overall seemingly too restrictive Nature of the Lores coupled with the counterintuitive progression of powerlevels within said Lores.<br /> <br /> I`ve read Devils Due after this, but I`m not a fan of how it is handled there, being too far removed from most of the other systems around.<br /> At the moment, I`m tending more to a flexible Version of the lores, similar to how DA:Fae handles the dominions, with the permanent Torment of the demon working als the &quot;Unleashing-Pool&quot; and the tormented variants of the powers occuring, whenever a spell goes haywire.<br /> <br /> The reason I lay this unripe idea out for you is, that I`d like your thoughts on the matter.<br /> How would you handle the powers of the fallen to represent their kind better?<br /> Would you condense two or more original Lores into a single demonic dominion (maybe Lore of Transfiguration and Lore of Flesch into a &quot;dominion&quot; of Flesch or something along those lines)?<br /> <br /> Any constructive Idea or criticism is highly apreciated. ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T06:46:46-08:00","id":781683,"title":"","content":"My current idea is not to change the Lores themselves significantly, but to allow demons to create derivative powers known as knacks.<br /> <br /> The system for using an evocation is different, simply roll your Lore rating plus one of your virtues. I'm currently toying between virtues and permanent faith, I like the themetics of using faith but it makes it too powerful.<br /> <br /> The second part is based off of my view of Lores. In specific that they aren't inherent Elohim powers but 'exploits of the computer code that is creation.' Therefore Fallen are able to experiment and come up with other uses for their knowledge, for a measly few XP.<br /> <br /> I don't know how unleashing in DA: Fae work, but if they are similar to CtD's cantrips I can see it working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T07:56:02-08:00","id":784745,"title":"","content":"Basically a DA:Fae has &quot;Dominions&quot; who cover a more or less loosly defined number of principles not unlike a mages sphere.<br /> For example the Dominion of Night covers Darkness, Fear, Ice and Shadow.<br /> For an unleashing, the player tells the GM, what kind of effect he wishes within his dominion and the GM tells him, what level of the dominion is necessary to pull it off.<br /> If the player has that level, he rolls Mists+Dominion (for Changeling think of a permanent Glamour roll) against a difficulty determined by the GM and a lot of situational or seasonal modifiers (Night Magic is more difficult during day and easyer at midnight for example).<br /> The GM rolls 5 Dice difficulty 6. Thouse are called &quot;unleashing-dice&quot;.<br /> If the player gets more sucesses than the GM all is well and the effect goes off as intended with all the sucesses counting.<br /> The more sucesses the GM rolls, the more &quot;magical&quot; the sideeffects of the unleashing are.<br /> If the GM scores more sucesses than the Fae, the spell goes haywire in a blast of uncontrolled magical energy of the flavour of the used Dominion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6112,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","user":"Seki","date":". 12-12-2015, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T22:07:13-08:00","id":786507,"title":"","content":"I originally felt this way, but with the addition of rituals and clear rules for relics, and the way you can buy Visage powers, I am inclined to stick with the current system. Visage powers grants you tricks like being able to trade in Faith for extra turns, be immune to flame or electricity, fly, lower difficulties, heal the bashing damage of others, manifest natural weaponry, and according to the author many other things that couldn't be covered due to space restrictions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T05:11:04-08:00","id":816787,"title":"","content":"Has anyone else any more ideas on how to handle this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T15:39:31-08:00","id":817214,"title":"","content":"WHO HAS SUMMON THE POWERFUL AND MIGHT CROWLEY?!<br /> oh, sup seki. Hey mercurial, hows a going.<br /> <br /> Ok first OFF, im typing from my cellphone. So sorry if all is a bit fucked up.<br /> <br /> But i dm em more in The Spheres (MtAs) attunement but more bind to The original Nature of The Fallen. Thats The long Story short","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T00:28:08-08:00","id":817456,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1754_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1754\" data-vbnamecard=\"1754\">Crowley</a> That sounds fascinating.<br /> I don`t suppose you could elaborate on that in more detail?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Here is how I am trying to house-rule them at the moment (still early work in progress, far from being playable):<br /> <br /> The 23 Lores are condensed into 12 Demonic Dominions (still searching for a good name).<br /> The &quot;Dominions&quot; of Life, Death, Heart, Soul, Paths, Fate, Flesh, Creation, Heaven, Earth, Ocean and Inferno.<br /> <br /> Basically each Dominion is a rough combination of two Lores (sometimes more, sometimes less).<br /> Some Lores are splitt between several of the dominions: Lore of Humanity of example has divided its powers into the dominion of Heart (governing emotions and Illusions) and the dominion of soul (governing mind control ond posession).<br /> <br /> The demon, in his apocalyptic form can unleash said dominions similar to how a DA:Fae can unleash their magic, with the permanent Torment of the demon being used as the &quot;unleashing-pool&quot;.<br /> To unleash demonic dominions one has to spend a point of faith, and it can only be done, while in the apocalyptic form.<br /> <br /> For 3 EXP each the demon may learn an &quot;evocation&quot;, in the same general vein as a Fae can learn cantrips. Defined magical effects out of the dem. dom. that they could possibly unleash if they would so desire.<br /> The benefit of learning an evocation are three-fold:<br /> 1. the difficulty of the &quot;unleasching-pool&quot; goes up by one, making it less likely, that Torment will cloude their magic<br /> 2. While in apocalyptic form, the evocation does not require the expense of a faith-point to be cast<br /> 3. The demon is able to perform this kind of magic even when not in his apocalyptic form. It does require the expense of a faith point though.<br /> <br /> Of coure it is possible to both unleash and learn as an evocation the &quot;high-torment&quot; variant of each spell. Fore those there is no &quot;unleashing-pool&quot;, since the Torment already twists the spell. However the demon automatically gains a temporary point of Torment whenever he uses said spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:35:48-08:00","id":817836,"title":"","content":"Look for The DtF thread<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}